cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "pynlme: Nonlinear Mixed-Effects Models for Python"
version: 0.5.1
date-released: 2026-10-12
url: "https://github.com/willov/pynlme"
repository-code: "https://github.com/willov/pynlme"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Lövfors"
    given-names: "William"
keywords:
  - "nonlinear mixed-effects models"
  - "pharmacokinetics"
  - "pharmacodynamics"
  - "SAEM algorithm"
  - "Lindstrom-Bates"
  - "Python"
abstract: >
  pynlme fits nonlinear mixed-effects models in Python, e.g. for
  pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic analyses and ODE models. It provides
  MATLAB's nlmefit and nlmefitsa (Lindstrom-Bates, FO, FOCE and SAEM) and an
  R nlme/saemix-style interface, written in Python with NumPy and SciPy and
  validated against MATLAB R2023b, R nlme and R saemix.
